${\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3}{2x{ln}^{2}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x).$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x}\\cdot 4=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡8$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3}{2x{ln}^{2}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x))^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {(-{u}^{-1})|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{u})|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{2}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{2}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}(-\\frac{1}{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490242 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a7aff6-d1b2-5383-bb26-aa6363594b05" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Definite Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "588a64f8-b007-597a-90a1-13bc0deadb69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489726} {:answer/id #uuid "58d74548-f1c5-5c19-af0c-64a5b689a324" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489727} {:answer/id #uuid "64f36bf8-3759-5b50-8859-73b64d5b2c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{log}_{2}⁡3\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489752} {:answer/id #uuid "ae420e08-ae64-53a3-b2a8-a61252329c53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489897} {:answer/id #uuid "fba1a44c-3ac0-56fc-b34d-91572dd0f45a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58d74548-f1c5-5c19-af0c-64a5b689a324" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489727} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e61d7a6-a656-53b9-8d80-257f6bbc76cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "43a38f2f-26ab-5a55-9c36-de9ec5e565a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-31615" :question/problem "What is the value of ${\\int }_{4}^{8}\\frac{1}{x{log}_{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $4$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{8}\\frac{1}{x{log}_{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{4}^{8}\\frac{1}{{log}_{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490225 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a7aff6-d1b2-5383-bb26-aa6363594b05" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Definite Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16b7494e-bb79-5b12-9236-a587f999330d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489565} {:answer/id #uuid "1b976c74-2288-5edb-ac14-b1435c6814f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489578} {:answer/id #uuid "4a39aa0a-e274-5fb2-8704-b394c3cd5dd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489687} {:answer/id #uuid "65a94067-f449-5e05-8e2b-89087734bd4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489754} {:answer/id #uuid "7c3b6154-88e4-5ca3-9c7b-ddeffecf3bd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489798}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c3b6154-88e4-5ca3-9c7b-ddeffecf3bd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489798} :answer-field/id #uuid "3273c5e4-90f1-5aee-9f26-60f52ccd89f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "29e8aaaf-e383-5b29-a6be-9cfefb451c7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-31616" :question/problem "What is the value of ${\\int }_{5}^{25}\\frac{3}{x{log}_{5}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{5}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $5$ | $25$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{25}\\frac{3}{x{log}_{5}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{5}^{25}\\frac{1}{{log}_{5}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490321 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a7aff6-d1b2-5383-bb26-aa6363594b05" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Definite Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c6a9f60-c08f-5467-a283-a5c875e998cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489583} {:answer/id #uuid "311cb6a0-4004-536b-aff8-04d49cb5cc24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489625} {:answer/id #uuid "abe6da9b-8429-54a3-ba90-b2deefe451bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489892} {:answer/id #uuid "f50f90e5-5553-5d0c-bfdb-c4fbba7c5236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490044} {:answer/id #uuid "fc4aa3c7-4608-5feb-8e43-09317d7d8264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f50f90e5-5553-5d0c-bfdb-c4fbba7c5236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490044} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8df4958-daa0-55e3-96a1-d8edb4b2bd89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490173}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ee507cc2-c5c1-5dca-b8f8-28391520da63" :question/math-academy-id "q-49552" :question/problem "What is the value of ${\\int }_{e/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x}\\cdot 4=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e/4$ | ${e}^{3}/4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{e/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332750 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a7aff6-d1b2-5383-bb26-aa6363594b05" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Definite Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f292278-673c-5eba-880c-7cda055f8171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330511} {:answer/id #uuid "5dac8132-bf52-5344-825a-5d6616a1cdd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330784} {:answer/id #uuid "83aeb76a-c46c-5da9-b6b1-d3b2c07f5e3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331119} {:answer/id #uuid "884a0de8-2fb3-540c-834e-7021c6f3a3b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331163} {:answer/id #uuid "dc4580e3-6e2d-5fe8-9d8c-28fc47a327cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dac8132-bf52-5344-825a-5d6616a1cdd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330784} :answer-field/id #uuid "d90e8da3-8c2b-5ff0-aa8c-d768bd2f0c85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332582}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "06ae8c49-a573-55e1-8d24-c78494f9b5b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-49606" :question/problem "What is the value of ${\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | ${e}^{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
